{"seq":1206,"lane":"B","class":"wrong-evidence-home","severity":"serious","evidence":"1206.json e2: “Nvidia guided the current quarter to $108 billion.” B links this company-wide figure to both v2, total revenue, and v10, Data Center revenue.","rule":"D207 and the signed standard §§5–6: file a statement under the narrowest open question it bears on.","mechanism":"B links the company-wide guidance to the segment question even though the passage gives no segment figure; v2 directly asks for total revenue."}
{"seq":1207,"lane":"drop","class":"fiscal-year-drop","severity":"serious","evidence":"1207.json c1: “What year-over-year total revenue growth will NVIDIA report for FY2028?” was dropped because “year 2028 is beyond next year”.","rule":"Signed standard §§3–4: a company's annual quantity uses its fiscal year and may cover the current or next fiscal year.","mechanism":"Record preparation returned bare “2028”, which the confirmation run treated as a calendar year. split-v2-design.md §6 records a subsequent correction; the stored confirmation trace still shows the drop."}
{"seq":1207,"lane":"B","class":"unhelpful-revenue-link","severity":"serious","evidence":"1207.json e3: “CME Group plans to launch futures on Oct. 5 tied to the hourly rental cost of Nvidia's H100 and B200 graphics processors, pending regulatory approval.” It was linked to v2, FY2027 total revenue.","rule":"Signed standard §§5.1 and 5.3: a kept statement must help answer a question; D273 and D361 retain the revenue fallback for relevant demand, supply, competition or pricing.","mechanism":"B appears to apply the broad revenue fallback to an announcement of a proposed trading instrument without identifying how that announcement changes the revenue outcome."}
{"seq":1207,"lane":"B","class":"unhelpful-revenue-link","severity":"serious","evidence":"1207.json e5: “Nvidia's revenue and hyperscaler capex tell you what's been booked; the compute curve tells you what's actually being consumed and what someone will pay for it a year out,” was linked to v2, FY2027 total revenue.","rule":"Signed standard §§5.1 and 5.3: general background without a concrete development that helps answer the question is not kept.","mechanism":"B treats an explanation of what a future market could indicate as evidence about the company's revenue, without an actual curve or change in demand."}
{"seq":1208,"lane":"B","class":"unsupported-official-attribution","severity":"serious","evidence":"1208.json e2: the article says “Also announced recently is a $12.9 billion acquisition of AI specialist Hugging Face.” The summary says “NVIDIA recently announced a $12.9 billion acquisition of Hugging Face” and assigns original_who “NVIDIA” and tier “fact”.","rule":"Signed standard §§2 and 5.4: preserve the original speaker and the evidential nature of the statement; do not turn an inference into a sourced fact.","mechanism":"B inferred that NVIDIA made the announcement, although the sentence does not identify who announced it. This stronger attribution also reaches matching."}
{"seq":1208,"lane":"matching","class":"invented-statement-date","severity":"serious","evidence":"1208.json e2 has original_day “”; matching returns “replace” against e4002 with said_day “2026-08-29”.","rule":"D203: an unknown original statement day stays unknown; D202 requires a later account for a revision.","mechanism":"src/hivemind/views/jev_matching.py:265 substitutes the article publication day when original_day is empty, exposing the replacement decision to an unsupported date."}
{"seq":1209,"lane":"A","class":"missing-new-question","severity":"serious","evidence":"1209.json: “Nvidia expects around 70% revenue growth next fiscal year, well above what Wall Street expected.” A opens only the supply-commitment question; the earlier FY2028 revenue-growth candidate was dropped at seq 1207.","rule":"Signed standard §§3–4: a value-driving company quantity for the next fiscal year can open when no existing question covers that annual outcome.","mechanism":"A did not propose the FY2028 revenue question despite receiving the current library and a forecast for that year. The trace does not establish why."}
{"seq":1209,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"unusable-question","severity":"serious","evidence":"1209.json v70 asks “How much has NVIDIA committed to memory and advanced-packaging supply through 2032, as disclosed by its FY2027 annual report?” It was written with due_day “”, rungs [] and judgements [].","rule":"Signed standard §§3–4 and D210: an assumed obligation opens as an amount with five outcomes and a check at the next annual report.","mechanism":"The preparation request permits an empty date and an empty ladder when it finds no reference; build_handover accepts both and writes the question. The trace does not establish that a precise ladder can be derived from this article."}
{"seq":1209,"lane":"B","class":"wrong-population-evidence","severity":"serious","evidence":"1209.json e4: “Nvidia’s CFO Colette Kress expects the top five hyperscalers to spend nearly $800 billion on capital spending in 2026. In 2027? Over $1.3 trillion.” It is linked to v4 and v5, which ask for four hyperscalers' data-center capital expenditure.","rule":"Signed standard §5.4: preserve the population and what a figure measures; D259 permits related-population evidence without making the populations identical.","mechanism":"B links the five-company, total-capital-spending forecast to the four-company, data-center-spending questions without establishing the difference in coverage. The retained summary preserves the five-company wording, but the links leave the comparison to the reader."}
{"seq":1210,"lane":"A","class":"missing-new-question","severity":"serious","evidence":"1210.json: “Kress spoke about 70% total revenue growth in fiscal 2028”; A proposes no questions, and the FY2028 revenue-growth candidate from seq 1207 was not opened.","rule":"Signed standard §§3–4: a value-driving company quantity for the next fiscal year can open when no existing question covers that annual outcome.","mechanism":"A did not propose the FY2028 revenue question despite the explicit forecast and the absence of that question from the library. The trace does not establish why."}
{"seq":1210,"lane":"B","class":"quote-summary-mismatch","severity":"serious","evidence":"1210.json handover e1 quotes “During second-quarter earnings, Nvidia CFO Colette Kress revealed that the company will be spending $279 billion on supply commitments over the next few years -- up from $119 billion only three months earlier. The reason for the jump is primarily about memory.” Its one_line additionally says “with $92 billion due in the rest of FY2027 and $87 billion and $88 billion in FY2028 and FY2029, respectively”.","rule":"Signed standard §2: a record carries a verbatim passage and a standalone summary of that statement.","mechanism":"B combined separated passages into one quote; source_quote retained the intact opening passage, while build_handover kept the longer summary unchanged. The additional amounts occur elsewhere in the article, but not in the retained quote."}
{"seq":1210,"lane":"drop","class":"quote-refusal","severity":"serious","evidence":"1210.json b6: “The bulk of Nvidia's memory spend will almost certainly land between SK Hynix and Micron Technology.” Handover drops it as “B quote absent from sent article”; the article contains the same sentence with stock tickers inserted after the two company names.","rule":"Signed standard §5.1 and D209: a helpful statement for an existing question should be kept; D236 and D266 require storage of the exact source passage.","mechanism":"source_quote does not reconcile the intervening stock-ticker markup with B's otherwise faithful quotation. The author's estimate is lost from v29, the question about a memory-supply commitment with SK Hynix."}
{"seq":1210,"lane":"B","class":"wrong-obligation-scope","severity":"serious","evidence":"1210.json e1: “the company will be spending $279 billion on supply commitments over the next few years ... The reason for the jump is primarily about memory.” It is filed under v70, “How much has NVIDIA committed to memory and advanced-packaging supply through 2032”.","rule":"Signed standard §5.4: preserve what a figure measures and its scope; §5.1 requires a link that helps answer the question.","mechanism":"B treats the broader total for supply commitments as though it measured the memory-and-advanced-packaging subset. “Primarily” does not establish that the full $279 billion belongs to that subset."}
{"seq":1211,"lane":"B","class":"wrong-evidence-home","severity":"serious","evidence":"1211.json e9: “Within the data center book, hyperscale customers contributed $48.7 billion of revenue -- an increase of 102% year over year” was linked to v2, total revenue, rather than v10, Data Center revenue.","rule":"D207 and signed standard §§5–6: file helpful evidence under the narrowest open question it bears on.","mechanism":"B selected the broad company-revenue question even though the passage expressly identifies the narrower segment."}
{"seq":1211,"lane":"B","class":"wrong-evidence-home","severity":"serious","evidence":"1211.json e7: “Operating income rose 19% sequentially and 124% year over year to $63.7 billion” was linked to v13, “What profit will NVIDIA report for FY2027?”, but not v25, “What operating margin will NVIDIA report for FY2027?”","rule":"Signed standard §5.1 and D259: retain figures that help answer an existing question; D207 calls for the narrowest applicable question.","mechanism":"B did not connect operating income to the operating-margin question, even though the same article supplies total revenue needed to interpret the figure."}
{"seq":1211,"lane":"record_preparation","class":"unusable-question","severity":"serious","evidence":"1211.json v71 asks “What gross margin will NVIDIA report for FY2028?” and was written with due_day “”, rungs [] and judgements []; the source says margin is expected to bottom “between 71% and 72% by the fourth quarter before recovering in fiscal 2028”.","rule":"Signed standard §§3–4 require five outcomes and a check date for an annual quantity. The preparation request permits a recent or part-year figure as a stated comparison.","mechanism":"Record preparation left the ladder empty despite receiving the near-term margin outlook; build_handover accepts an empty ladder and date."}
{"seq":1211,"lane":"B","class":"wrong-obligation-scope","severity":"serious","evidence":"1211.json e15: “Nvidia's commitments for critical components increased from $119 billion last quarter to $279 billion,” “primarily related to the procurement of memory.” It is filed under v70's memory-and-advanced-packaging amount.","rule":"Signed standard §5.4: preserve the scope of a reported figure.","mechanism":"B files a total for critical components as evidence for the narrower memory-and-advanced-packaging amount without establishing how much of the total belongs to that subset."}
{"seq":1211,"lane":"matching","class":"same-article-evidence-duplicated","severity":"serious","evidence":"1211.json: “Kress told investors that Nvidia's commitments for critical components increased from $119 billion last quarter to $279 billion, saying it was ‘primarily related to the procurement of memory.’” _ledger.json stores it as e4229 under v71 and e4241 under v70.","rule":"Signed standard §2 and D250: one research matter in one article is one record; a record can link to relevant questions.","mechanism":"A and B independently return the same passage. The handover and writer store the two outputs separately rather than reconciling the same article's statement into one record with its applicable links."}
{"summary":{"items_read":[1205,1206,1207,1208,1209,1210,1211,1212],"classes":{"wrong-evidence-home":3,"fiscal-year-drop":1,"unhelpful-revenue-link":2,"unsupported-official-attribution":1,"invented-statement-date":1,"missing-new-question":2,"unusable-question":2,"wrong-population-evidence":1,"quote-summary-mismatch":1,"quote-refusal":1,"wrong-obligation-scope":2,"same-article-evidence-duplicated":1}}}